  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1242 PM MDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\n\nFor tomorrow night, a slug of moisture will move across western \nColorado. This will impact mainly the western slope tomorrow night \nand this area will see a good chance of showers and storms. Some of \nthese showers will push out into the Sangre De Cristo mtns. It \nshould remain dry over the plains tomorrow night.\n\nFor Monday, major weather changes begin to occur. It will likely \nremain showers over the divide throughout the entire day. These \nshowers will then push eastward over the remainder of the mtns and \nvalleys during the afternoon. Additionally during the afternoon time \nperiod, showers are expected to develop over the plains along a \ntrough that will continue to be located from roughly the Kim to \nsouth of Lamar region. \n\nBY late Monday afternoon, a rather strong cold front will begin to \nenter the area from the north and push across the region during the \nevening hours. This front marks the leading edge of cooler air that \nwill move into the region Monday night. Shower may last over the \nplains during the evening hours.\n\nTuesday, much cooler weather is expected to prevail with mid 70s to \nlower 80s over the plains for max temps. Tuesday may be one of those \ndays that it may be too stable for precip to occur over the plains \nduring the day, but showers and thunderstorms will be widespread \nduring the day across the mountains and valleys, with the heaviest \nprecip likely occuring along the mountains/plains interface as moist \nupslope flow combines with the monsoon flow to bring a favorable \npattern for heavy rain. Likewise, the chance for burn scar flooding \nover the Aspen Acres burn scar will be on the increase during this \nperiod. \n\nFor Tuesday evening, scattered to likely showers and storms are \nexpected region-wide, with the activity continuing into the late \nnight hours over the far eastern plains.\n\nWednesday will be a bit warmer, but scattered to numerous shower and \nstorms are expected over the region during the afternoon and evening \nhours. \n\nAnother reinforcing cool front will move into the region Wednesday \nnight, and this will help continue the chance of showers and storms \nover the region into Thursday. Showers are forecast to be less \nnumerous for Friday. \\/Hodanish",
